      "text": "Correct Answer: $\\pi$\nDistribute the $\\sin x$ to each term of the expression inside the sum. Since $\\sin^2 x = \\sin^2 x$, the term is divided by $\\sin x$. Similarly, $\\cos^2 x \\div \\cos x = \\cos x$. $\\sin x = \\pm \\cos x$. The equation of the curve is simplified as: $y = \\sin x \\cos x + \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}$. We substitute the value of the argument of the sin function into the equation. According to the condition, the expression $\\frac{x - \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} + k\\pi \\right) }{2}$ can be regarded as the argument of the sin function, where $k \\in \\mathbb{Z}$. Therefore, the solution to the problem is as follows: $\\boxed y = \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\tan x$. The period of the curve is $2\\pi$.\n\nNote: In fact, the argument of the sum of trigonometric functions is a linear function of $x$. If $A(x) + B(x)$ satisfies this condition, the period of $f(x) = A(x) + B(x)$ is $\\boxed{AB}$.",
